# Astra UI rules

1. Reuse `components/astra` before creating a new visual primitive.
2. Do not use arbitrary colors when a design token exists (`canvas`, `surface`, `ink`, `muted`, `line`, semantic states).
3. Do not use arbitrary radius values. Prefer `radius-control` (6px) or none.
4. Avoid gradients and glassmorphism.
5. Do not create giant KPI cards.
6. Prefer typography + spacing over nested boxes.
7. Summary first, reasoning second, evidence on demand.
8. Do not expose raw JSON by default.
9. Do not expose raw backend enums when readable labels exist.
10. Do not invent numbers.
11. Do not hardcode benchmark results.
12. Do not hardcode selected products.
13. Do not put business logic in React.
14. Backend remains the source of truth.
15. Do not create Presentation Mode, Demo Mode, Judge Mode, or Pitch Mode.
16. Technical detail belongs in Inspector/Drawer (`AstraInspector`).
17. Status cannot depend on color alone. Use `AstraStatusBadge` (includes a text tone label).
18. Use `AstraSourceBadge` for provenance.
19. Use `AstraStatusBadge` for state.
20. Prefer dense enterprise layouts over decorative cards.
21. Use motion only when it explains state change. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
22. Keep LIVE as the primary visual experience.

shadcn primitives in `components/ui` are implementation details. Feature pages should import Astra components, not raw `Badge`/`Card` with one-off classes.
